    {# BODY #}
    <article class="mt-6">
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
        The press conference for <a href="/en/movie/ikatan-darah/" class="text-uwais-red underline underline-offset-4">Ikatan Darah Film</a> recently captured the attention of both the public and the national film industry. 
        This latest action film starring Iko Uwais and directed by Tata Sidharta introduces a different approach to action storytelling, 
        with a level of production quality that has already received recognition on the international stage.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
        Beyond delivering intense action sequences, the film also carries a strong emotional message through its story and deeply developed characters.
      </p>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          The Director’s Idealism and a Distinct Visual Vision
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          During the press conference, director Tata Sidharta revealed that "Ikatan Darah" was born from an idealistic vision to create an Indonesian action film that is not only visually spectacular but also strong in storytelling.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          According to him, creative discussions with Iko Uwais played an important role in shaping the film. 
          They agreed that every fight sequence must carry emotional meaning that supports the development of the characters.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          Through this approach, the film aims to demonstrate that martial arts action can serve as a powerful medium for conveying emotions, conflicts, and deeper character journeys.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          A Prestigious Journey: From American Film Festivals to Indonesia
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          One of the exciting announcements made during the press conference was the film’s international journey. 
          Before its scheduled release in Indonesia, "Ikatan Darah" had already been screened at several prestigious film festivals in the United States.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          The film received positive responses from international critics, particularly for its cinematography and highly realistic action choreography.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          This achievement proves that productions from Uwais Pictures are capable of competing in the global market while raising expectations among Indonesian audiences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          Extreme Physical Challenges and Realistic Action Choreography
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          As the lead actor and action choreographer, Iko Uwais explained that the production demanded exceptional physical preparation. 
          All cast members were required to undergo months of intensive training to ensure every action scene appeared authentic. 
          The use of stunt performers was also minimized to deliver a more realistic action experience.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          Iko emphasized that every movement was carefully designed to look dangerous on screen while still being performed under strict safety standards for the cast and production crew.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          Strong On-Set Chemistry Among the Cast
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          Despite the intense action sequences, the atmosphere behind the scenes was filled with warmth. 
          The cast members built strong relationships through simple activities during the production process, including script discussions, training sessions, and shared meals.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          This closeness ultimately translated into the dynamic interactions between characters in the film, both in emotional dramatic scenes and during intense physical confrontations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          A Social Mission: Inspiring the Younger Generation
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          More than just entertainment, the film carries a powerful social message. 
          Iko Uwais hopes that "Ikatan Darah" will inspire Indonesia’s younger generation to channel their energy into more positive pursuits.
          Through the film, he aims to introduce values such as discipline, hard work, and creativity—qualities that can be developed through martial arts and the film industry.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          His hope is that the film will inspire young people to move away from negative influences and start pursuing their passions in a productive way.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-medium text-white mb-3">
          Official Trailer and Poster Release for Ikatan Darah
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          The press conference concluded with the launch of the film’s official poster and latest trailer. 
          The footage showcased various brutal action sequences with cinematic visuals and a dark atmosphere, while the dramatic background music intensified the tension in every scene.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-uwais-muted">
          For fans of action films similar to "The Raid" but with a more mature dramatic approach, "Ikatan Darah" is predicted to become one of the most highly anticipated Indonesian films of the year.
        </p>
      </section>

